Package: tsintermittent
Type: Package
Title: Intermittent Time Series Forecasting
Version: 2.0
Date: 2026-11-08
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nikolaos", "Kourentzes", email = "nikolaos@kourentzes.com", role = c("cre","aut"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0211-5218")),
    person("Fotios", "Petropoulos", email = "F.Petropoulos@bath.ac.uk", role = "ctb", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3039-4955")))
Description: Time series methods for intermittent demand forecasting. Includes Croston's method and its variants (Moving Average, SBA), and the TSB method. Users can obtain optimal parameters on a variety of loss functions, or use fixed ones (Kourentzes (2014) <doi:10.1016/j.ijpe.2014.06.007>). Intermittent time series classification methods and iMAPA that uses multiple temporal aggregation levels are also provided (Petropoulos & Kourentzes (2015) <doi:10.1057/jors.2014.62>). Empirical quantiles of the demand over the lead time are calculated from the cumulative forecast errors (Saoud, Kourentzes & Boylan (2022) <doi:10.1016/j.omega.2022.102614>).
